CM_ "Transport-visibility reference DBC for tests/io614_can_visibility_test.
Signal bit layout follows inverter_hil/inverter_hil_plan.md section 4 as
INSPIRATION ONLY: exact bit positions/scales are NOT verified against a
physical capture, and the torque scale is a placeholder (1/512 Nm/count,
matching the provisional profile used elsewhere in inverter_hil; the
plan also documents a competing 1/256 Nm/count reading that is unresolved,
see inverter_hil_plan.md section 4.1.1). The io614_can_visibility_test
Simulink model itself uses raw IO614 CAN Read/Write blocks, not this DBC,
and makes no claim about payload semantics -- see
io614_can_visibility_test_plan.md, 'Minimal model behavior'. Copy/replace
this file with the canonical inverter_hil.dbc once that project produces
one (see inverter_hil_plan.md section 2/4 and this test's Open decisions).";
CM_ BO_ 390 "VCU control frame to Ephorus channel 1 (0x186).";
CM_ BO_ 406 "VCU control frame to Ephorus channel 2 (0x196).";
CM_ BO_ 422 "VCU control frame to Ephorus channel 3 (0x1A6).";
CM_ BO_ 438 "VCU control frame to Ephorus channel 4 (0x1B6).";
CM_ BO_ 899 "Ephorus channel 1 3X3 status (0x383). Also the PCAN smoke-test
default tx_id in io614_can_visibility_test_plan.md; the smoke test does
not decode these signals, it only checks raw ID/DLC/payload transport.";
